    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 🧠 Theory: Types of Memory\n",
    "\n",
    "Agents need memory to:\n",
    "1. **Remember** what happened in the conversation\n",
    "2. **Track** task progress\n",
    "3. **Store** collected information\n",
    "\n",
    "### Memory Types\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n",
    "│             AGENT MEMORY TYPES                       │\n",
    "├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n",
    "│                                                     │\n",
    "│  1. CONVERSATION MEMORY                            │\n",
    "│     - Chat history                                 │\n",
    "│     - Previous messages                            │\n",
    "│                                                     │\n",
    "│  2. WORKING MEMORY / STATE                         │\n",
    "│     - Current task context                         │\n",
    "│     - Collected data                              │\n",
    "│                                                     │\n",
    "│  3. LONG-TERM MEMORY                               │\n",
    "│     - Persistent storage                          │\n",
    "│     - User preferences                             │\n",
    "│                                                     │\n",
    "│  4. TOOL MEMORY                                    │\n",
    "│     - Results from tool calls                       │\n",
    "│                                                     │\n",
    "└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 💻 Conversation Memory\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's implement basic conversation memory:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from langchain_core.messages import AIMessage, HumanMessage\n",
    "from langchain_openai import ChatOpenAI\n",
    "\n",
    "# Without memory - each conversation is fresh\n",
    "llm = ChatOpenAI(model=\"gpt-4o-mini\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# First turn\n",
    "print(\"📍 Turn 1: No memory\")\n",
    "response1 = llm.invoke(\"My name is Alice.\")\n",
    "print(f\"   User: My name is Alice.\")\n",
    "print(f\"   AI: {response1.content}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Second turn - but it doesn't know!\n",
    "print(\"\\n📍 Turn 2: No memory\")\n",
    "response2 = llm.invoke(\"What's my name?\")\n",
    "print(f\"   User: What's my name?\")\n",
    "print(f\"   AI: {response2.content}\")\n",
    "print(\"   ⚠️ The AI forgot!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# With conversation memory\n",
    "from langchain.memory import ConversationBufferMemory\n",
    "from langchain.chains import ConversationChain\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create memory\n",
    "memory = ConversationBufferMemory(memory_key=\"history\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create conversation chain\n",
    "conversation = ConversationChain(\n",
    "    llm=llm,\n",
    "    memory=memory,\n",
    "    verbose=True\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# First turn\n",
    "response1 = conversation.predict(input=\"My name is Alice.\")\n",
    "print(f\"   User: My name is Alice.\")\n",
    "print(f\"   AI: {response1}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Second turn - it remembers!\n",
    "response2 = conversation.predict(input=\"What's my name?\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\n   User: What's my name?\")\n",
    "print(f\"   AI: {response2}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### How Conversation Memory Works\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n",
    "│          CONVERSATION MEMORY                        │\n",
    "├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n",
    "│                                                     │\n",
    "│  Messages:                                        │\n",
    "│  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────  │\n",
    "│  Human: My name is Alice.                          │\n",
    "│  AI: Nice to meet you, Alice!                     │\n",
    "│  Human: What's my name?                          │\n",
    "│  [System adds previous messages to context]       │\n",
    "│  AI: Your name is Alice!                          │\n",
    "│                                                     │\n",
    "└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 📊 Agent State Management\n",
    "\n",
    "Agents need to track more than chat - they need **state**:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from dataclasses import dataclass, field\n",
    "from typing import List, Dict, Any\n",
    "\n",
    "# Define agent state\n",
    "@dataclass\n",
    "class AgentState:\n",
    "    \"\"\"State for a research agent.\"\"\"\n",
    "    task: str = \"\"\n",
    "    collected_info: List[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n",
    "    current_step: int = 0\n",
    "    completed: bool = False\n",
    "    errors: List[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Example: Research agent state\n",
    "state = AgentState(\n",
    "    task=\"Research AI trends 2024\",\n",
    "    current_step=2\n",
    ")\n",
    "state.collected_info.append(\"Found: GPT-5 announced\")\n",
    "state.collected_info.append(\"Found: New Claude model released\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"📦 Agent State\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 60)\n",
    "print(f\"Task: {state.task}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Step: {state.current_step}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Collected info:\")\n",
    "for info in state.collected_info:\n",
    "    print(f\"  • {info}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Completed: {state.completed}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Errors: {state.errors}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### State in LangGraph\n",
    "\n",
    "LangGraph uses stateful graphs - let's see how it works:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from langgraph.graph import StateGraph, END\n",
    "from typing import TypedDict\n",
    "\n",
    "# Define state schema\n",
    "class ResearchState(TypedDict):\n",
    "    \"\"\"State for research agent.\"\"\"\n",
    "    query: str\n",
    "    results: list\n",
    "    summary: str\n",
    "    iteration: int\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create graph\n",
    "graph = StateGraph(ResearchState)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add nodes\n",
    "def search_node(state: ResearchState) -> ResearchState:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Search for information.\"\"\"\n",
    "    state['results'].append(f\"Search result for: {state['query']}\")\n",
    "    state['iteration'] += 1\n",
    "    return state\n",
    "\n",
    "def summarize_node(state: ResearchState) -> ResearchState:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Summarize results.\"\"\"\n",
    "    state['summary'] = f\"Found {len(state['results'])} results\"\n",
    "    return state\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add to graph\n",
    "graph.add_node(\"search\", search_node)\n",
    "graph.add_node(\"summarize\", summarize_node)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Define flow\n",
    "graph.set_entry_point(\"search\")\n",
    "graph.add_edge(\"search\", \"summarize\")\n",
    "graph.add_edge(\"summarize\", END)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Compile and run\n",
    "app = graph.compile()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Run\n",
    "result = app.invoke({\n",
    "    \"query\": \"AI trends\",\n",
    "    \"results\": [],\n",
    "    \"summary\": \"\",\n",
    "    \"iteration\": 0\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"📊 LangGraph State Flow\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 60)\n",
    "print(f\"Query: {result['query']}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Results: {result['results']}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Summary: {result['summary']}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Iterations: {result['iteration']}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 💾 Persistence\n",
    "\n",
    "For real apps, you'll want to persist state:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import json\n",
    "\n",
    "# Simple file-based persistence\n",
    "class SimpleAgentMemory:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Simple file-based memory.\"\"\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def __init__(self, filepath=\"agent_memory.json\"):\n",
    "        self.filepath = filepath\n",
    "        self.state = self._load()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def _load(self) -> dict:\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            with open(self.filepath, 'r') as f:\n",
    "                return json.load(f)\n",
    "        except FileNotFoundError:\n",
    "            return {\"history\": [], \"data\": {}}\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def save(self):\n",
    "        with open(self.filepath, 'w') as f:\n",
    "            json.dump(self.state, f)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def add_message(self, role: str, content: str):\n",
    "        self.state[\"history\"].append({\"role\": role, \"content\": content})\n",
    "        self.save()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def get_history(self) -> list:\n",
    "        return self.state[\"history\"]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def set_data(self, key: str, value: any):\n",
    "        self.state[\"data\"][key] = value\n",
    "        self.save()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def get_data(self, key: str) -> any:\n",
    "        return self.state[\"data\"].get(key)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test it\n",
    "mem = SimpleAgentMemory(\"test_memory.json\")\n",
    "mem.add_message(\"user\", \"Hello!\")\n",
    "mem.add_message(\"assistant\", \"Hi there!\")\n",
    "mem.set_data(\"task_status\", \"in_progress\")\n",
    "mem.set_data(\"steps_completed\", 3)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✅ Memory saved!\")\n",
    "print(f\"History: {mem.get_history()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Task status: {mem.get_data('task_status')}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Steps: {mem.get_data('steps_completed')}\")"
   ]
  },
